00:10:42,089 --> 00:10:44,229
[Tom]
Oops. Somebody flushed.

242
00:10:44,264 --> 00:10:45,679
[George] That's right.
There she is.

243
00:10:45,714 --> 00:10:47,232
Oh, yeah.

244
00:10:47,267 --> 00:10:50,511
[Tom]
Oh, I get it. He's got cable.

245
00:10:52,272 --> 00:10:55,102
There she is.

246
00:10:55,137 --> 00:10:56,621
It's fanne fox.

247
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,105
[Tom] No, it's
a maxfield Parrish painting.

248
00:10:58,140 --> 00:10:59,693
[Joel]
You're both right.
It's fanne fox

249
00:10:59,728 --> 00:11:01,488
in a maxfield Parrish painting.

250
00:11:01,522 --> 00:11:03,732
Both jokes can work together.
Let's watch on.

251
00:11:03,766 --> 00:11:05,043
[Tom]
Okay.

252
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:09,738
Hey, mom! Hey, mom, watch me!
Watch this!

253
00:11:09,772 --> 00:11:11,532
[Imitating bubbles bubbling]

254
00:11:11,567 --> 00:11:15,847
Gidget goes
to the renaissance festival.

255
00:11:15,882 --> 00:11:19,023
- I hope the cold water has
soothed your temper, my lady.
- That's precise editing, huh?

256
00:11:19,057 --> 00:11:22,233
- No, I'm just as furious
as ever.
- I am furious yellow.

257
00:11:22,267 --> 00:11:24,097
Oh, it's easy enough
for you to talk.

258
00:11:24,131 --> 00:11:25,788
You can do
whatever you please.

259
00:11:25,823 --> 00:11:28,032
Fall in love,
fall out of it again.

260
00:11:28,066 --> 00:11:30,103
A squire one day,
a stable boy the next.

261
00:11:30,137 --> 00:11:31,725
I get the point.
All right. Geez.

262
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:33,451
I might as well be
a prisoner in a tower.

263
00:11:33,485 --> 00:11:37,006
I can't even speak to a man
let alone have him look at me.

264
00:11:37,041 --> 00:11:39,733
It's the penalty
of being a Princess.

265
00:11:39,768 --> 00:11:42,460
But even a Princess
should be allowed romance.

266
00:11:42,494 --> 00:11:43,979
[Tom]
Even cowgirls get the blues.

267
00:11:44,013 --> 00:11:46,740
- How will I ever meet him?
- [Woman] Who, my lady?

268
00:11:46,775 --> 00:11:49,881
- The one I could love.
- Think that's
her natural color?

269
00:11:49,916 --> 00:11:51,296
You'll have
your chance someday.

270
00:11:51,331 --> 00:11:53,643
- She has been hitting
the dye pods.
- You run along.

271
00:11:53,678 --> 00:11:56,716
- But your gown.
- I'll dress myself.

272
00:11:56,750 --> 00:11:58,027
Well, then, what will you do?

273
00:11:58,062 --> 00:12:00,823
Oh, what I always do--
sit here and dream.

274
00:12:00,858 --> 00:12:03,861
[Joel]
"Sit there and drink"?

275
00:12:03,895 --> 00:12:05,897
- [Tom] No. "Dream."
- Oh.

276
00:12:05,932 --> 00:12:07,968
[Sybil]
Princess helene.

277
00:12:08,003 --> 00:12:09,936
[Tom]
Your lights are on.

278
00:12:11,661 --> 00:12:13,042
Who are you?

279
00:12:13,077 --> 00:12:15,976
[Joel] Just came
to freak you out, baby.

280
00:12:16,011 --> 00:12:17,806
What do you want?

281
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:20,187
[Joel]
This doesn't do anything
for you?

282
00:12:20,222 --> 00:12:22,120
- Come on. I'm a ghost.
- Stay away.

283
00:12:22,155 --> 00:12:24,778
- Marcia Wallace?
- Oh!

284
00:12:24,813 --> 00:12:26,366
Don't you come any closer.

285
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:29,852
No, Princess.
I'm going to take care of you.

286
00:12:32,234 --> 00:12:35,030
She's stuck.
Bang her on the side
of the head there.

287
00:12:35,064 --> 00:12:36,963
2,000 flushes.

288
00:12:36,997 --> 00:12:40,587
- Helene. Helene!
- [Tom] "Fillet"?

289
00:12:40,621 --> 00:12:42,623
- [Joel] Gary lockwood.
- It is.

290
00:12:44,142 --> 00:12:46,696
[Joel] Check this out.
"Open the pod bay doors, hal."

291
00:12:46,731 --> 00:12:49,113
- [Tom] Good one.
- [Laughs] 'Cause it's... yeah.

292
00:12:49,147 --> 00:12:52,599
[Tom] Mommy, mommy, mommy,
there's a scary
flushing thing, and it...

293
00:12:52,633 --> 00:12:56,016
- Sybil, where are you?
- You needn't shout, George.

294
00:12:56,051 --> 00:12:58,294
- [Joel] Endora!
- I can hear you.

295
00:12:58,329 --> 00:13:00,296
I must leave here.
She's in danger.

296
00:13:00,331 --> 00:13:03,230
Who in the netherworld
are you talking about?

297
00:13:03,265 --> 00:13:06,233
Princess helene.
I loved her from
the first moment I saw her.

298
00:13:06,268 --> 00:13:09,789
[Laughs]
A reflection in the water,
and you fall in love.

299
00:13:09,823 --> 00:13:12,170
- You silly child.
- Last week,
it was a deck of cards.

300
00:13:12,205 --> 00:13:13,689
Something terrible
has happened to her.

301
00:13:13,723 --> 00:13:16,174
Let me see what
you're talking about.

302
00:13:18,694 --> 00:13:22,146
Magic mirror,
show me what has upset my boy.

303
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:24,838
Adolescence, puberty,
raging hormones.

304
00:13:24,873 --> 00:13:26,667
The Princess is gone,
your majesty.

305
00:13:26,702 --> 00:13:28,842
She's not in her quarters,
not in the garden,
not by the pool.

306
00:13:28,877 --> 00:13:30,706
Yet no one saw her
leave the palace.

307
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:32,225
[Tom] Well, she works late
on Tuesdays, you know.

308
00:13:32,259 --> 00:13:34,020
Then turn out the guards,
sir branton.

309
00:13:34,054 --> 00:13:36,885
We have done that.
Until she is found,

310
00:13:36,919 --> 00:13:38,990
no one will be permitted
in or out of the palace.

311
00:13:39,025 --> 00:13:42,338
- Well, he's wearing fighting...
- ♪♪ [trumpet fanfare]

312
00:13:43,788 --> 00:13:46,515
Can't you just walk into
the room without a big to-do?

313
00:13:46,549 --> 00:13:47,896
[Tom]
♪ to-do

314
00:13:47,930 --> 00:13:49,829
[whispering]
He played Sherlock Holmes,
that one.

315
00:13:49,863 --> 00:13:51,589
Who is this?

316
00:13:51,623 --> 00:13:54,212
We found him skulking
within the eastern postern.

317
00:13:54,247 --> 00:13:56,628
- I wasn't skulking.
I was hanging around.
- He won't speak.

318
00:13:56,663 --> 00:13:58,389
There are means
to make him speak.

319
00:13:59,459 --> 00:14:00,805
[Thunderclap]

320
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:03,877
Oh, no. Not a solo.

321
00:14:03,912 --> 00:14:06,224
- Sir branton.
- [Tom] Neat.

322
00:14:06,259 --> 00:14:08,709
Your most serene majesty,

323
00:14:08,744 --> 00:14:10,677
you can call off the search.

324
00:14:10,711 --> 00:14:12,782
The Princess, your daughter,
is in my castle,

325
00:14:12,817 --> 00:14:14,198
under lock and key.

326
00:14:14,232 --> 00:14:16,648
- Well, as long as
she's sa-- hey!
- Who are you?

327
00:14:16,683 --> 00:14:19,789
- Lodac.
- The sorcerer?

328
00:14:19,824 --> 00:14:22,896
- [Joel] No!
Of course it's the sorcerer!
- [Lodac, indistinct]

329
00:14:22,931 --> 00:14:27,211
Lodac, you say my daughter
is at your castle?

330
00:14:27,245 --> 00:14:29,109
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.
- But why?

331
00:14:29,144 --> 00:14:32,112
How have I hurt you?
Why have you done this thing?

332
00:14:32,147 --> 00:14:34,977
The answer is very simple.

333
00:14:35,012 --> 00:14:37,462
Your father executed my sister
for witchcraft

334
00:14:37,497 --> 00:14:39,223
when she was only
18 years old.

335
00:14:39,257 --> 00:14:40,741
- [Joel] Painful.
- [Lodac] I have waited

336
00:14:40,776 --> 00:14:43,089
until your daughter
reached that age

337
00:14:43,123 --> 00:14:44,918
so that my dragon

338
00:14:44,953 --> 00:14:47,921
could relish the flesh
of the Princess.

339
00:14:47,956 --> 00:14:49,750
- [Joel] Oh, wow.
- I beseech you--

340
00:14:49,785 --> 00:14:52,512
- beseech nothing.
- [Tom] Yeah, beseech this.

341
00:14:52,546 --> 00:14:55,273
[Branton]
You have this worm-eaten
sorcerer frighten US?

342
00:14:55,308 --> 00:14:57,344
- [King] Be careful, branton.
- [Branton] Not I.

343
00:14:57,379 --> 00:14:59,864
- Lodac...
- [Joel] You're a jerk.

344
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,176
I shall find your castle,

345
00:15:01,210 --> 00:15:03,143
free the Princess
and see you destroyed.

346
00:15:03,178 --> 00:15:05,076
All while balancing
an egg on a spoon.

347
00:15:05,111 --> 00:15:06,906
Finding my castle
is no great task.

348
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:09,287
- [Tom] Hey, mc lyte
wants her necklace back.
- It's a short journey.

349
00:15:09,322 --> 00:15:11,117
You simply follow
the yellow star of north.

350
00:15:12,739 --> 00:15:14,465
The trick is...

351
00:15:14,499 --> 00:15:16,950
How to get there... alive.

352
00:15:16,985 --> 00:15:19,504
- I shall.
- I'm afraid not.

353
00:15:25,994 --> 00:15:27,961
[Thunderclap]

354
00:15:27,996 --> 00:15:30,653
[Tom, as if over radio]
Uh, Houston, we have liftoff.
Over.

355
00:15:30,688 --> 00:15:32,828
[Echoing]
...That lies between
this castle and mine.

356
00:15:32,862 --> 00:15:34,450
[Thunderclap]

357
00:15:34,485 --> 00:15:36,452
- He's got a reverb pedal.
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

358
00:15:36,487 --> 00:15:40,146
- Let no man live
who dares the dark journey.
- [Thunderclap]

359
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:44,564
Let no man face
my seven curses
and reach the dragon's lair.

360
00:15:44,598 --> 00:15:48,602
[Joel]
You ain't woman enough
to take my man.

361
00:15:48,637 --> 00:15:53,193
- Your curses won't stop me
from reaching your castle.
- Fem for all seasons here.

362
00:15:53,228 --> 00:15:56,645
The Princess helene
will make a delicate dish
for my dragon--

363
00:15:56,679 --> 00:15:58,474
I'm serving her over rice
with fava beans.

364
00:15:58,509 --> 00:16:00,235
- [Slurping]
- ...In exactly
seven days' time.

365
00:16:00,269 --> 00:16:04,135
And now,
if you'll excuse me.

366
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:06,862
- Uh, wait. Was that
seven days starting now?
- [Thunderclap]

367
00:16:06,896 --> 00:16:10,141
- Or is it seven days st--
- [Joel] Take me. I'm yours.

368
00:16:10,176 --> 00:16:11,487
- [Caws]
- Ooh.

369
00:16:11,522 --> 00:16:14,007
[Screechy voice]
Nevermore! Nevermore!

370
00:16:14,042 --> 00:16:16,216
[Tom] Oh, suppose that
could've gone better.

371
00:16:16,251 --> 00:16:19,012
Sir branton,
my daughter will die.

372
00:16:19,047 --> 00:16:21,946
No, sire,
for I will rescue her.

373
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:23,672
You'll risk the seven curses?

374
00:16:23,706 --> 00:16:26,019
- [Laughs]
I love that carlin bit.
- For helene, I'd risk 70.

375
00:16:26,054 --> 00:16:28,263
The man who saves helene

376
00:16:28,297 --> 00:16:30,506
will have her hand in marriage
and half my kingdom.

377
00:16:30,541 --> 00:16:32,957
- Check it out.
She looks like Ronald McDonald.
- Trust me, sire.

378
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,648
[Whispers]
No one's supposed to know.

379
00:16:34,683 --> 00:16:37,858
Oh, no! It is I
who must save the Princess,
not sir branton!

380
00:16:37,893 --> 00:16:39,205
- [Mocking gibberish]
- I love her.

381
00:16:39,239 --> 00:16:42,070
Do you think I'd let you
face lodac's sorcery?

382
00:16:42,104 --> 00:16:44,486
- [Joel] You don't have
your lerner's permit.
- I'm not afraid.

383
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:46,660
300 years ago,
my father and brother

384
00:16:46,695 --> 00:16:48,662
were devoured
by lodac's dragon.

385
00:16:48,697 --> 00:16:53,150
- Oh, not this story again.
- And my family were great
sorcerers in their own right.

386
00:16:53,184 --> 00:16:56,222
- I remember it like
it was 200 years ago.
- They were no match for lodac.

387
00:16:56,256 --> 00:16:57,982
I am no match for lodac.
I confess it.

388
00:16:58,017 --> 00:17:01,503
- Okay, okay!
- I fear him almost as much
as I hate him.

389
00:17:01,537 --> 00:17:03,505
- But, Sybil, i--
- please, I gesticulate you!

390
00:17:03,539 --> 00:17:06,059
[Sybil] You will stay
right here at home
where you are safe.

391
00:17:06,094 --> 00:17:09,062
- [Joel] You're grounded.
- You can have
anything you want,

392
00:17:09,097 --> 00:17:10,581
but you're staying here.

393
00:17:10,615 --> 00:17:13,377
All I want is my freedom
so I can save the girl I love!

394
00:17:13,411 --> 00:17:15,206
[Tom] All I want
is what's coming to me!

395
00:17:15,241 --> 00:17:17,415
But you wouldn't
understand that,
not being mortal!

396
00:17:17,450 --> 00:17:18,934
Oh, that hurt.

397
00:17:18,968 --> 00:17:21,143
I tried to do my best.

398
00:17:22,489 --> 00:17:24,457
Oh, I know you have, Sybil.

399
00:17:24,491 --> 00:17:26,183
[Sybil]
Can't you call me mother?

400
00:17:26,217 --> 00:17:29,013
[Joel]
Oh, is it "mother" today?

401
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,463
I'm sorry, mother.

402
00:17:30,497 --> 00:17:33,431
You were only a week old

403
00:17:33,466 --> 00:17:36,193
when your royal parents
died from the plague.

404
00:17:36,227 --> 00:17:38,505
- Those were happier times.
- I found you,

405
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:40,197
reared you as my own son.

406
00:17:40,231 --> 00:17:42,026
Must have the answers
written on his hand.

407
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:43,510
You've been kind and loving.

408
00:17:43,545 --> 00:17:45,719
- I'd do anything for you.
- [Tom] Flaking.

409
00:17:45,754 --> 00:17:47,756
But I can't stay here
with you anymore.

410
00:17:47,790 --> 00:17:50,103
[Joel]
It's weird!

411
00:17:50,138 --> 00:17:52,864
I'm not a child.
I'm 20, and I love helene.

412
00:17:54,245 --> 00:17:57,145
Talk to me of love
when you're 420.

413
00:17:57,179 --> 00:18:01,010
When you're human,
20 is old enough
to feel love and misery.

414
00:18:01,045 --> 00:18:04,117
- Give me my freedom.
- [Joel] Okay,
but it's not wrapped.

415
00:18:04,152 --> 00:18:07,914
I must say you're being
very difficult tonight.

416
00:18:07,948 --> 00:18:11,193
- Oh, well. Boys will be boys.
- In the hood.

417
00:18:11,228 --> 00:18:13,885
[Sybil]
We'll have to cheer you up.

418
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:15,266
Watch mother now.

419
00:18:15,301 --> 00:18:18,200
[Imitates squelching sound]

420
00:18:18,235 --> 00:18:20,202
[Joel] I'm gonna have
a big bowl of kwisp.

421
00:18:20,237 --> 00:18:22,860
- [Tom] Mmm. Food.
- Get that lady
a saucer and milk.

422
00:18:22,894 --> 00:18:24,724
- [Purrs]
- Not that trick again.

423
00:18:26,691 --> 00:18:28,003
- [Tom] Again?
- [Laughing]

424
00:18:28,037 --> 00:18:30,764
Does he have a cotton panel
in those briefs?

425
00:18:30,799 --> 00:18:32,766
- George!
- [Tom] Don't ya know me?

426
00:18:32,801 --> 00:18:35,183
I've never seen you
like this before.

427
00:18:35,217 --> 00:18:37,461
Look, if you'll cheer up,

428
00:18:37,495 --> 00:18:39,532
forget about
that girl and lodac,

429
00:18:39,566 --> 00:18:42,190
I'll let you see
the presents

430
00:18:42,224 --> 00:18:44,640
I've chosen for you
when you're 21.

431
00:18:44,675 --> 00:18:48,023
- [Joel] A new codpiece?
- [Tom] Mm.

432
00:18:48,057 --> 00:18:49,507
What sort of presents, mother?

433
00:18:49,542 --> 00:18:51,199
Come along.

434
00:18:51,233 --> 00:18:53,166
♪ To Alexander's ragtime band

435
00:18:53,201 --> 00:18:55,237
I'll show you.

436
00:18:55,272 --> 00:18:58,275
Packed with peanuts,
estelle really satisfies.

437
00:18:58,309 --> 00:18:59,690
Oh, yes.

438
00:18:59,724 --> 00:19:01,692
♪♪ [Humming]

439
00:19:05,074 --> 00:19:06,490
♪♪ [Humming continues]

440
00:19:06,524 --> 00:19:07,974
♪♪ [Whistling]

441
00:19:09,596 --> 00:19:11,909
[Clears throat]

442
00:19:11,943 --> 00:19:13,186
[Tom]
Hey.

443
00:19:13,221 --> 00:19:16,638
[Joel] "Why do you seek
the living among the dead"?

444
00:19:18,226 --> 00:19:21,539
Carol merrill,
what's behind that curtain?

445
00:19:21,574 --> 00:19:23,092
- Like leno.
- [Tom] It's a new horse!

446
00:19:23,127 --> 00:19:26,095
[Imitating audience cheering]

447
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:27,442
Do you like him?

448
00:19:27,476 --> 00:19:29,789
[Joel] Geez, any kid would.
He's swell!

449
00:19:29,823 --> 00:19:31,618
He's magnificent.

450
00:19:31,653 --> 00:19:33,482
[Sybil]
He's yours when you're 21.

451
00:19:33,517 --> 00:19:35,588
His name is beyhar.

452
00:19:35,622 --> 00:19:37,555
He's no ordinary animal.

453
00:19:37,590 --> 00:19:39,488
- He's your father.
- [Sybil] Possesses magic.

454
00:19:39,523 --> 00:19:41,663
This is the fastest horse
in all the world.

455
00:19:41,697 --> 00:19:46,115
- [Joel]
♪ I am Mr. Edgar winter
- no other steed can beat him.

456
00:19:46,150 --> 00:19:49,498
[Tom] And it can all be yours
if the price is right.

457
00:19:50,672 --> 00:19:52,708
- Take the door.
- No, go for the curtain!

458
00:19:52,743 --> 00:19:55,159
- Take the curtain!
- Ohh!

459
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,574
[Chuckles]

460
00:19:56,609 --> 00:19:59,232
- A candy striper's outfit?
Thanks, mom!
- Wow!

461
00:19:59,267 --> 00:20:00,820
See this?

462
00:20:00,854 --> 00:20:02,477
You'll wear it
when you ride the stallion.

463
00:20:02,511 --> 00:20:04,133
Used to be your sister's.

464
00:20:04,168 --> 00:20:06,550
Does this armor
possess magic too?

465
00:20:06,584 --> 00:20:08,207
No weapon can Pierce it.

466
00:20:08,241 --> 00:20:10,036
[Tom]
Except a butter knife.

467
00:20:10,070 --> 00:20:12,452
And this is ascalon,

468
00:20:12,487 --> 00:20:14,109
the blade.

469
00:20:14,143 --> 00:20:16,042
None like it
since the world began.

470
00:20:16,076 --> 00:20:19,218
- It defies all swords
in metal.
- [Joel] It's a ginsu 2000!

471
00:20:19,252 --> 00:20:21,806
Black magic is overcome
by a touch of the blade.

472
00:20:21,841 --> 00:20:25,224
So there.
All yours when you are 21.

473
00:20:25,258 --> 00:20:27,605
- If the price is right.
- And I'll let you
go after lodac

474
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:30,539
for my revenge
as well as your own.

475
00:20:30,574 --> 00:20:33,577
With the help of their magic,
I could save the Princess now.

476
00:20:33,611 --> 00:20:35,613
No. You're not old enough.

477
00:20:35,648 --> 00:20:38,202
You wouldn't know
how to use them.

478
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:41,205
- No, don't touch it.
Don't even look at it.
- Just let me hold it.

479
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,862
Just to get the feel of it.

480
00:20:42,896 --> 00:20:45,209
Please? Just for awhile.

481
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:47,176
[Chuckles]
Very well.

482
00:20:51,595 --> 00:20:52,630
[Tom]
Hmm.

483
00:20:52,665 --> 00:20:55,046
It feels like a part
of my own body.

484
00:20:55,081 --> 00:20:57,773
- So it's like your arm?
- I feel stronger.

485
00:20:57,808 --> 00:20:59,844
- Of course.
- More confident, dry, secure.

486
00:20:59,879 --> 00:21:01,190
Now come along.

487
00:21:01,225 --> 00:21:04,124
It pleases me to show you
something else tonight.

488
00:21:04,159 --> 00:21:06,126
[Joel]
Boss, it's a Hank Aaron model.

489
00:21:10,165 --> 00:21:12,443
- Who are they?
- The village people.

490
00:21:12,478 --> 00:21:14,583
[Sybil]
The six most Valiant knights
in the world.

491
00:21:14,618 --> 00:21:17,206
[Joel] That's him, officer.
Third from the left.

492
00:21:17,241 --> 00:21:19,208
[George]
It's real black magic, mother.

493
00:21:19,243 --> 00:21:21,487
- [Sybil] I wish
I could take the credit.
- ♪ that old black magic

494
00:21:21,521 --> 00:21:23,903
I've never been as good as that.
No, it was my brother.

495
00:21:23,937 --> 00:21:26,215
- Do you like ascalon?
- Geez, mom, all this stuff
was in my room,

496
00:21:26,250 --> 00:21:28,873
- ...and I never
noticed it before.
- It's just great.

497
00:21:28,908 --> 00:21:31,669
- Now I can be the prep cook
I always wanted to be.
- [Clang]

498
00:21:31,704 --> 00:21:32,981
[Rumbling]

499
00:21:34,707 --> 00:21:36,433
- [Gasps]
- Ooh.

500
00:21:36,467 --> 00:21:38,193
[Tom] Oh, now I've done it.
Sorry, mom.

501
00:21:41,921 --> 00:21:44,199
- Did the sword do that?
- Sure did, Jethro.

502
00:21:44,233 --> 00:21:46,960
One touch of the blade,
and it opens and shuts

503
00:21:46,995 --> 00:21:49,204
floors, doors, walls
and portcullises.

504
00:21:49,238 --> 00:21:52,207
- And it snaps caps off jugs,
bottles and jars.
- Shuts things, too, you say.

505
00:21:52,241 --> 00:21:55,797
[Tom]
What the hell. Hmm.

506
00:21:55,831 --> 00:21:57,661
- What's down there?
- [Tom] China.

507
00:21:57,695 --> 00:22:00,042
I haven't been down there
in centuries.

508
00:22:00,077 --> 00:22:02,562
Used to be my brother's
safe-deposit box

509
00:22:02,597 --> 00:22:05,669
for spells, enchantments,

510
00:22:05,703 --> 00:22:07,671
magic ritual and the like.

511
00:22:07,705 --> 00:22:10,984
- Want to see?
- [Joel] Old magazines
and my high school yearbook.

512
00:22:11,019 --> 00:22:13,711
Is there any other way out
if the crack were closed again?

513
00:22:13,746 --> 00:22:16,404
- There's the kitchen door.
- Depends how hard
you work at it.

514
00:22:16,438 --> 00:22:19,061
- A cousin of mine
took 80 years...
- Oh, boy.

515
00:22:19,096 --> 00:22:21,823
...to whomp up a spell
that blew the roof off.

516
00:22:21,857 --> 00:22:26,206
- But don't be afraid.
- She's got more stories about
her relatives than Gabe kaplan.

517
00:22:26,241 --> 00:22:29,071
Oh, I'm not afraid.

518
00:22:29,106 --> 00:22:30,797
Uh, you go first, mother.

519
00:22:30,832 --> 00:22:32,178
[Sybil]
Hmm.

520
00:22:32,212 --> 00:22:33,490
[Tom]
"Hmm."

521
00:22:33,524 --> 00:22:35,215
Age before beauty, I guess.

522
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:37,217
- Hey.
- Whoa-ho!

523
00:22:37,252 --> 00:22:40,566
- I didn't wanna see that.
- ♪ one singular sensation

524
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:42,706
- coming, dear?
- [George] Yes.

525
00:22:48,470 --> 00:22:49,885
[Tom]
Hey...

526
00:22:52,232 --> 00:22:53,958
- [Clang]
- [Joel] Psyche!

527
00:22:53,993 --> 00:22:55,788
- [Sybil] George!
- [Tom] My toe!

528
00:22:55,822 --> 00:22:58,273
[Sybil]
George, what have you done?
George, let me out!

529
00:22:58,307 --> 00:22:59,895
Good-bye, mother.

530
00:22:59,930 --> 00:23:03,209
[Sybil]
George, son,
let me out this instant!

531
00:23:03,243 --> 00:23:05,970
You can't leave me here.
I told you about my cousin.

532
00:23:06,005 --> 00:23:09,767
I'll come back and let you out
after I've rescued
the Princess helene.

533
00:23:09,802 --> 00:23:11,735
- [Sybil shouting]
- [Tom] I'll go hungry by then.

534
00:23:11,769 --> 00:23:14,496
With the magic armor,
magic sword,

535
00:23:14,531 --> 00:23:16,187
- ...magic steed--
- and my refrigeration
certificate--

536
00:23:16,222 --> 00:23:17,913
-...what can stop me now?
- ...From pine city vo-tech.

537
00:23:17,948 --> 00:23:20,191
[Sybil]
You don't know, George!

538
00:23:20,226 --> 00:23:22,193
George, let me out!

539
00:23:22,228 --> 00:23:24,195
- [Tom mimicking sobs]
- [Joel scoffs]

540
00:23:24,230 --> 00:23:25,818
- Taffeta!
- [Tom] Let's go.

541
00:23:25,852 --> 00:23:28,096
[Joel] Hey. Basil rathbone--
that gives me an idea.

542
00:23:28,130 --> 00:23:31,133
- Remember those doggie
costumes you had?
- Oh, yeah.

543
00:23:42,248 --> 00:23:46,079
- [Barking]
- You know, you get outta
your dog what you put into it.

544
00:23:46,114 --> 00:23:47,909
[Female voice]
Top trainer, Joel Robinson.

545
00:23:47,943 --> 00:23:51,084
And I only put in the best--
basil rathbones.

546
00:23:51,119 --> 00:23:52,845
Okay, crow. Okay.

547
00:23:52,879 --> 00:23:55,261
- [Whining]
- Okay, boy, wait for it.
Wait for it.

548
00:23:55,295 --> 00:23:57,021
Good!
[Laughs]

549
00:23:57,056 --> 00:23:59,507
You know, a top-trained dog
like this one

550
00:23:59,541 --> 00:24:01,992
is a lot like any of US people,
you know?

551
00:24:02,026 --> 00:24:04,581
We all need affection,
occasional grooming,

552
00:24:04,615 --> 00:24:07,100
and lots and lots of snacks.

553
00:24:07,135 --> 00:24:10,587
And dogs just go nuts
for the rich taste
of basil rathbone.

554
00:24:10,621 --> 00:24:15,108
One rathbone a day
will clean doggy's teeth
and freshen doggy breath.

555
00:24:15,143 --> 00:24:17,490
- And they're packed with bits
of Nigel Bruce.
- Mm-hmm.

556
00:24:17,525 --> 00:24:19,561
Hey, these are too good
to be good for you.

557
00:24:19,596 --> 00:24:22,461
- Okay, Tom servo, you sit.
- [Whining]

558
00:24:22,495 --> 00:24:24,601
Sit. Oh, good doggy.

559
00:24:24,635 --> 00:24:27,707
[Laughs]
Basil rathbones.

560
00:24:27,742 --> 00:24:31,608
And Pesto-flavored
basil rathbones
for the pretentious dog.

561
00:24:31,642 --> 00:24:33,506
Now in grass and stick flavor.

562
00:24:33,541 --> 00:24:35,508
It's alimentary,
my dear Robinson,

563
00:24:35,543 --> 00:24:37,614
to love basil rathbones!

564
00:24:37,648 --> 00:24:40,202
Oh-ho-ho!
Have my doggies been good?

565
00:24:40,237 --> 00:24:42,722
- [Growling]
- Oh, they are such
good doggies.

566
00:24:42,757 --> 00:24:44,690
Do the doggies want to go out?

567
00:24:50,558 --> 00:24:53,181
♪♪

568
00:24:53,215 --> 00:24:55,632
- We bring you tennis balls,
your majesty.
- Woof.

569
00:24:55,666 --> 00:24:57,737
Your majesty,
these knights and I

570
00:24:57,772 --> 00:25:00,257
have come to serve you
in your hour of need.

571
00:25:00,291 --> 00:25:03,432
- That's very kind.
- [Tom] But we're not hungry
right now.

572
00:25:03,467 --> 00:25:04,917
I am sir George,

573
00:25:04,951 --> 00:25:07,506
a knight by virtue
of 400 years of nobel lineage.

574
00:25:07,540 --> 00:25:09,991
- And a degree from
cardinal strict college.
- [King, indistinct]

575
00:25:10,025 --> 00:25:11,751
These are my comrades in arms.

576
00:25:11,786 --> 00:25:13,753
- Sir Dennis of France.
- [Joel mutters]

577
00:25:13,788 --> 00:25:15,755
[Speaks in French]

578
00:25:15,790 --> 00:25:18,137
- He's gonna have
really bad hat hair.
- Oh, yeah.

579
00:25:18,171 --> 00:25:20,070
[George]
Sir ulrich of Germany.

580
00:25:20,104 --> 00:25:22,003
Meinkaiser, we come to serve.

581
00:25:22,037 --> 00:25:24,177
- [Joel]
The voice of Paul frees!
- [George] Sir Anthony of Italy.

582
00:25:24,212 --> 00:25:27,422
- [Tom] Yo, Tony!
- [Speaks in Italian]

583
00:25:27,456 --> 00:25:29,182
- [Joel] Harry shearer!
- [George] Sir Pedro of Spain.

584
00:25:29,217 --> 00:25:32,876
- He's got an observatory
on his head.
- [Speaks in Spanish]

585
00:25:32,910 --> 00:25:34,533
[George]
Sir James of Scotland.

586
00:25:34,567 --> 00:25:37,190
Our hearts grieve for you
and your sorrow, your majesty.

587
00:25:37,225 --> 00:25:39,227
- [Tom] Hmm?
- [George] And last--

588
00:25:39,261 --> 00:25:40,608
[Joel]
Terry, the sensitive knight.

589
00:25:40,642 --> 00:25:42,195
[George]
...Sir Patrick of Ireland.

590
00:25:42,230 --> 00:25:43,990
We pledge our lives
to your service

591
00:25:44,025 --> 00:25:45,992
and to the Princess helene
until she's safe.

592
00:25:46,027 --> 00:25:48,201
What, is he the knight
from the Bronx?

593
00:25:48,236 --> 00:25:51,791
Gentlemen,
speaking for the king,
we are grateful for your offer.

594
00:25:51,826 --> 00:25:55,277
I am sure that you can be
of immeasurable service
to his majesty while I'm away.

595
00:25:55,312 --> 00:25:57,763
-We'll keep your resumés
on file.
-That's not what Patrick meant,

596
00:25:57,797 --> 00:26:01,007
- ...sir branton.
- Oh, you know who I am.
Have we met?

597
00:26:01,042 --> 00:26:03,596
- Oh, I've often seen you.
- That's an old line.

598
00:26:03,631 --> 00:26:06,081
- In the field?
- Not in the field.

599
00:26:06,116 --> 00:26:08,567
And they also know you wish
to marry the Princess helene.

600
00:26:08,601 --> 00:26:12,122
Oh, quite true.
You're all welcome to stay
and dance at my wedding.

601
00:26:12,156 --> 00:26:13,675
- Yeah, me and what army?
- Many thanks.

602
00:26:13,710 --> 00:26:16,160
- [Tom] Oh.
- But I prefer to dance
at my own.

603
00:26:16,195 --> 00:26:18,197
- We're getting into
a weird area here.
- [Indistinct]

604
00:26:18,231 --> 00:26:21,200
Don't try to solve them
till we've rescued
the Princess helene.

605
00:26:21,234 --> 00:26:23,098
"We"?
[Chuckles]

606
00:26:23,133 --> 00:26:26,067
- [Joel] What do you mean "we,"
kemo sabe?
- I shall rescue helene.

607
00:26:26,101 --> 00:26:28,448
Monsieur, try to understand.

608
00:26:28,483 --> 00:26:32,176
We are all sworn to save
sir George's beautiful lady.

609
00:26:32,211 --> 00:26:34,178
- Sir George's lady?
- [Tom] I think what our bright

610
00:26:34,213 --> 00:26:36,456
young French friend
is trying to say is...

611
00:26:36,491 --> 00:26:38,666
What does the frenchman mean?

612
00:26:38,700 --> 00:26:40,806
Only that I love her,
and I intend to marry her.

613
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:43,740
- Oh, okay. What-- hey!
- You arrogant boy.

614
00:26:43,774 --> 00:26:45,845
Do you know the perils
of the dark journey?

615
00:26:45,880 --> 00:26:47,675
We do, sir branton.

616
00:26:47,709 --> 00:26:49,193
If you don't share
our enthusiasm,

617
00:26:49,228 --> 00:26:50,643
we shall be happy
to go on without you.

618
00:26:50,678 --> 00:26:51,817
- [Joel laughs]
- Okay.

619
00:26:51,851 --> 00:26:52,921
Oh!

620
00:26:52,956 --> 00:26:54,440
Your majesty,
have I your permission

621
00:26:54,474 --> 00:26:56,684
to give this stripling
a lesson in the use of arms?

622
00:26:56,718 --> 00:26:59,203
- Permission to cut him
in half, sir.
- I shall not draw.

623
00:26:59,238 --> 00:27:02,172
- [Tom] I shall paint.
- Except in behalf
of Princess helene.

624
00:27:02,206 --> 00:27:04,795
A coward. Draw!

625
00:27:07,418 --> 00:27:09,662
- [People gasping]
- [Joel] You jerk!
You broke my sword!

626
00:27:09,697 --> 00:27:11,008
[Murmuring]

627
00:27:11,043 --> 00:27:12,527
Enough. That's enough.

628
00:27:12,561 --> 00:27:16,289
Sir branton,
I like these knights.

629
00:27:16,324 --> 00:27:18,775
- Surely there's safety
in numbers.
- You violated ape law.

630
00:27:18,809 --> 00:27:20,880
You and seven good swords.

631
00:27:20,915 --> 00:27:22,813
Seven swords?

632
00:27:22,848 --> 00:27:24,435
[Tom]
For seven brothers.

633
00:27:24,470 --> 00:27:25,851
And seven curses.

634
00:27:25,885 --> 00:27:27,197
[Tom]
For seven brothers.

635
00:27:27,231 --> 00:27:29,544
When do we start, sir branton?

636
00:27:29,578 --> 00:27:32,167
- Now.
- Mark, get set, go!

637
00:27:32,202 --> 00:27:33,755
[Joel]
Haikeeba!

638
00:27:33,790 --> 00:27:36,171
Aahhh.

639
00:27:36,206 --> 00:27:38,795
[Tom]
And a double haikeeba.

640
00:27:38,829 --> 00:27:41,590
[Mutters]

641
00:27:41,625 --> 00:27:44,179
- ♪ Knights in white satin
- ♪♪ [Joel humming along]

642
00:27:44,214 --> 00:27:46,388
♪ Never reaching the...

643
00:27:47,769 --> 00:27:51,773
[Tom] Come on, you ragtag
bunch of misfits.

644
00:27:51,808 --> 00:27:53,879
Whoo! I'm glad I don't
have to mow that lawn.

645
00:27:53,913 --> 00:27:55,846
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.
- It's like a golf course.

646
00:27:59,608 --> 00:28:00,989
Hmm?

647
00:28:01,024 --> 00:28:02,922
[Joel]
Tonight on mime court...

648
00:28:02,957 --> 00:28:06,995
Yeah, if you're really bad,
they throw you
in the imaginary box.

649
00:28:07,030 --> 00:28:09,791
[Joel]
Petticoat dungeon.

650
00:28:09,826 --> 00:28:11,172
I'm helene.

651
00:28:11,206 --> 00:28:12,656
We know.

652
00:28:12,691 --> 00:28:14,796
We heard you were brought in
this morning.

653
00:28:14,831 --> 00:28:17,834
I'm Princess Laura,
and this is my sister grace.

654
00:28:17,868 --> 00:28:19,456
This is our seventh day.

655
00:28:19,490 --> 00:28:21,527
- Let's form a girl group.
- Seventh day?

656
00:28:21,561 --> 00:28:23,805
Our last day, unless...

657
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:26,497
- [Tom] Aw.
- Surely you don't believe that
about the dragon.

658
00:28:26,532 --> 00:28:30,156
There were others here
when we arrived,
but they're gone now.

659
00:28:30,191 --> 00:28:31,813
Georgette, everybody.

660
00:28:31,848 --> 00:28:34,713
Then your father will do
something to save you.

661
00:28:34,747 --> 00:28:37,681
His army is probably
approaching the castle
this very minute.

662
00:28:37,716 --> 00:28:39,683
- Do you really think so?
- Don't kid yourself, sister.

663
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:41,858
- We've been here
for seven years.
- Of course.

664
00:28:41,892 --> 00:28:43,756
You'll be on your way home
by morning.

665
00:28:43,791 --> 00:28:45,758
[Dragon growling]

666
00:28:45,793 --> 00:28:47,933
Oh, that's my dad.

667
00:28:47,967 --> 00:28:50,176
[Growling continues]

668
00:28:50,211 --> 00:28:51,764
[Keys jingling]

669
00:28:51,799 --> 00:28:53,145
[Footsteps]

670
00:28:54,215 --> 00:28:56,251
Hmm?

671
00:28:56,286 --> 00:28:57,770
The two sisters.

672
00:28:57,805 --> 00:29:00,255
[Tom] ♪ there were never
such devoted sisters ♪

673
00:29:00,290 --> 00:29:02,188
- Eraserhead.
- [Joel] Literally.

674
00:29:02,223 --> 00:29:05,157
We're free to go home now?
Father arranged
for our release?

675
00:29:05,191 --> 00:29:07,538
You're not going home.

676
00:29:07,573 --> 00:29:09,748
- You're going to Disneyland.
- Surely you must have
spoken to him.

677
00:29:09,782 --> 00:29:13,717
I've had three long,
dull sessions with him,

678
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:16,237
but nothing could persuade him
to give up what I asked for.

679
00:29:16,271 --> 00:29:19,171
I don't believe you.
He'd pay you anything.

680
00:29:19,205 --> 00:29:20,759
[Lodac]
Nothing.

681
00:29:20,793 --> 00:29:22,691
Instead, he sent
an entire company

682
00:29:22,726 --> 00:29:24,970
of his bravest knights
on the dark journey.

683
00:29:25,004 --> 00:29:26,178
[Clicks tongue]

684
00:29:26,212 --> 00:29:29,077
The poor lads never even
reached the third curse.

685
00:29:29,112 --> 00:29:30,976
- Take them away.
- [Joel] They bore me.

686
00:29:31,010 --> 00:29:32,080
No! No!

687
00:29:32,115 --> 00:29:34,013
Can I take their
snoopy poster down now?

688
00:29:34,048 --> 00:29:35,912
- [Princess] No! Help! No!
- You can't do this.

689
00:29:35,946 --> 00:29:37,983
- [Princesses yelling]
- It just can't be happening.

690
00:29:38,017 --> 00:29:41,055
There just couldn't be anybody
as cruel and evil as you.

691
00:29:41,089 --> 00:29:43,160
- [Chuckling]
- No, I won't hear it.
There's a man in--

692
00:29:43,195 --> 00:29:46,163
this isn't the first time
that a Princess has been
fed to a dragon.

693
00:29:46,198 --> 00:29:48,821
And at least around here,
it happens only once a week.

694
00:29:48,856 --> 00:29:50,789
Unless you get what you want.

695
00:29:50,823 --> 00:29:52,791
What ransom
are you asking for me?

696
00:29:52,825 --> 00:29:55,103
I'm sorry,
but you happen to be
a particular case.

697
00:29:55,138 --> 00:29:57,934
I'm not asking any ransom
for you at all.

698
00:29:57,968 --> 00:29:59,936
Then why did you
bring me here?

699
00:29:59,970 --> 00:30:04,181
- My little pet will be hungry
